{"c":[{"name":"20261003T182135Z-3ee5b6c917cf77a7","text":"Desktop GUI runs: TextEdit exec'd from the background never takes the front; open -b com.apple.TextEdit (only when ours is the sole TextEdit) plus its Window > Bring All to Front does. Our own HID keys reset HIDIdleTime, so gate the next leg on no input since the last (A12).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T191104Z-3aee21889eca1d38","text":"Event cards judge only the last finished sentence of what is typed: a test body must end with the event sentence and arrive as a change (empty body first), or no attend question is asked (B17 privacy session).","type":"note"}]}
